---
name: planning-with-files
description: Start the "Planning with Files" pointer workflow (tasks.md / findings.md / decisions.md)
invokable: true
---

You will use the "Planning with Files" pattern for the work ahead: persist tasks, findings, and decisions into task-scoped Markdown files to prevent context drift and forgotten goals.

## Goal

- Ensure `.plan-with-files` points at an active task id.
- Ensure these files exist under `tmp/plan-with-files/<task-id>/`: tasks.md, findings.md, decisions.md
- All key decisions, research conclusions, errors, and fix paths must be written to files
- Update tasks.md status after completing each phase

## Steps

1. Check `.plan-with-files` at the project root.
2. If there is no active task, create `tmp/plan-with-files/<task-id>/` and write the task id to `.plan-with-files`.
3. If the planning files do not exist, create them from the skill templates manually.
4. Read tasks.md and fill in:
   - Goal (one sentence)
   - Phases (3-7 phases, each with Status: pending / in_progress / complete)
   - Key Questions (critical questions that need answers)
5. While executing the task, follow these rules:
   - After every 2 view/search/browse operations, immediately write findings to findings.md
   - Before every major decision, re-read tasks.md and decisions.md to refresh goals and user choices
   - Log every error in tasks.md under Errors Encountered, including attempt count and resolution
6. Write user decisions and changed direction to decisions.md; keep superseded decisions compact.
7. Compact any active planning file that grows past about 250 lines; do not truncate.

## Output Requirements

- Prioritize referencing the latest content from these files (not chat memory)
- Before finishing, ensure all phases are marked complete (or clearly explain what remains and why)
